;;; A macro's call inside a fact a query's claim lists loads, and the claim can never hold —
;;; M1f **W86**, register row `W86/macro-call-in-claim`, filed by S1f.7.12 (T1f.7.12.2, 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, a macro `settled`, the fact `(says (paid Ann))`, and a query over `says` whose
;;; claim lists `(says (settled Ann))`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A claim lists facts, and a fact is not expanded: the claim lists a fact no state can hold.
;;; Refused at load, at the call, one line, on every command. A claim headed by the call,
;;; `(model (settled Ann))`, names no relation of the program and has been refused since S1f.7.5
;;; (Q-M1f.118).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `91b12be8`, release: the program loads; the query has one class, `?c = (paid Ann)`, and
;;; the claim is FAILED, *the claim lists (model (says (settled Ann))), which is no class*: `ein
;;; solve` and `ein test` exit 1, every other command 0.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.12 (T1f.7.12.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Claim :why "it is said that {?1}")
(macro settled (?g) (paid ?g) :why "{?g} has settled: they have paid")
(says (paid Ann))
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (says ?c) :expect (model (says (settled Ann))))
